' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  ADM as a cyclic wheel vs a linear waterfall of the same phases.
'   usecase:      Teach the iterative intent of ADM vs a one-pass waterfall.
'   complexity:   variant
'   domain:       enterprise / architecture-method
' ============================================================================
title Example TOGAF ADM - Cycle vs Waterfall

note as TopNote
  Variant: same 8 phases shown TWO ways.
  TOP: ADM cyclic wheel - H feeds back into A (iterate).
  BOTTOM: linear waterfall - H ends; no feedback loop.
  The cycle encodes CONTINUOUS re-planning; the waterfall does not.
end note

' ============ TOP: CYCLIC WHEEL ============
usecase "A (cycle)" as cA
usecase "B (cycle)" as cB
usecase "C (cycle)" as cC
usecase "D (cycle)" as cD
usecase "E (cycle)" as cE
usecase "F (cycle)" as cF
usecase "G (cycle)" as cG
usecase "H (cycle)" as cH

cA --> cB --> cC --> cD --> cE --> cF --> cG --> cH
cH --> cA : iterate

' ============ BOTTOM: WATERFALL (linear, no loopback) ============
rectangle "A (waterfall)" as wA
rectangle "B (waterfall)" as wB
rectangle "C (waterfall)" as wC
rectangle "D (waterfall)" as wD
rectangle "E (waterfall)" as wE
rectangle "F (waterfall)" as wF
rectangle "G (waterfall)" as wG
rectangle "H (waterfall)" as wH

wA --> wB
wB --> wC
wC --> wD
wD --> wE
wE --> wF
wF --> wG
wG --> wH
note right of wH : STOP - no feedback to A
